.TH pr "" "Command"
.SH NAME
pr \- paginate and print files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpr [+\fIskip\fB] [\-\fIn\fB] [\-n] [\-h \fIheader\fB] [\-l\fIn\fB]
[\-m] [\-s\fIc\fB] [\-t] [\-w\fIn\fB] [\fIfile ...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
pr -- paginate and print files
Usage:	pr [ options ] [ file ... ]
Options:
	+n	Skip the first 'n' pages of input before printing
	-n	Print the input in 'n' columns
	-h	The next argument is the header (replaces file name)
	-ln	Page size is set to 'n' lines (default: 66)
	-m	Print each input 'file' in a separate column
	-sc	Separate each column with character 'c'
	-t	Suppress top and bottom margins and header
	-wn	Page width is set to 'n' columns (default: 80)
A 'file' named '-' means standard input.
.HE
.B pr
paginates each
.I file
and writes it to the standard output.
At the top of each page (unless
.B \-t
is given),
.B pr
writes a header giving today's date, the file's name (or the
.B \-h
header), the page number, and the input line number at which printing
of that page begins.
.PP
A
.I file
named
.B \-
means the standard input; if no
.I file
is given at all,
.B pr
also reads the standard input.
.PP
Options are recognized up to the first file name; each of the
following may be given:
.IP \fB+\fIn\fR
Skip the first
.I n
pages of input before printing begins.
.IP \fB\-\fIn\fR
A bare decimal number after the
.B \-
sets the number of output columns to
.IR n .
.IP \fB\-n\fR
Number each output line, in a 4-column field followed by a colon.
.IP "\fB\-h \fIheader\fR"
Use
.I header
in place of the file name in the page title.
If not attached directly to
.BR \-h ,
.I header
is taken as the next command-line argument (so a multi-word header
must be one shell argument, e.g. quoted).
.IP \fB\-l\fIn\fR
Set the page length to
.I n
lines (default 66).
.IP \fB\-m\fR
Print each input
.I file
in its own column, side by side; opens all the named files at once.
.IP \fB\-s\fIc\fR
Separate each column with the character
.IR c ;
if
.I c
is omitted, a tab is used.
.IP \fB\-t\fR
Suppress the top and bottom margins and the header.
.IP \fB\-w\fIn\fR
Set the page width to
.I n
columns (default 80).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B cat
.SH NOTES
.B pr
generates plain ASCII text; it has no notion of a page-description
output format.
